# AI development workflow

When implementing screens from Google Stitch:

1. Treat Stitch project `projects/5487252279778690236` and **Modern Cricket Club** (`assets/11807811405223687109`) as visual source of truth.
2. Pull / confirm screens via Stitch MCP before coding major UI.
3. Do not copy generated HTML.
4. Rebuild with reusable components from `src/components` and feature folders.
5. Keep dual token sources in sync (`globals.css` + `design-tokens.ts`).
6. Follow architecture: UI → Hook → Service → Repository → Supabase.
7. Reuse existing components first (`MatchTicket`, `SegmentedControl`, `BottomSheet`, typography).
8. Separate presentation from business logic — no Supabase / authz in JSX.
9. Preserve UX while improving maintainability; split files >250 lines.
10. Update `.cursor/rules` / `docs/UI.md` when the DS or signature patterns change.

Always explain non-obvious architectural decisions in brief code comments.
